From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Luke Craig <lacraig3@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 15:10:17 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] target/riscv: log hardware A/D page-table updates as dirty

With Svadu (or without Svade), get_physical_address() sets a PTE's A and D
bits with a cmpxchg through the host pointer of the page-table page. Nothing
logs that store: dirty-memory clients never see it, so live migration can
lose the update and in-memory snapshots that copy back only dirty pages leave
set A/D bits behind (the same bug target/arm/ptw.c had for FEAT_HAFDBS).
Mark the PTE's bytes dirty for the region's logging clients after a
successful update. DIRTY_MEMORY_CODE is excluded, so TB tracking is as before.
Only hardware A/D updates pay for it.
---
 target/riscv/tcg/cpu_helper.c | 11 +++++++++++
 1 file changed, 11 insertions(+)

diff --git a/target/riscv/tcg/cpu_helper.c b/target/riscv/tcg/cpu_helper.c
index 07d922265..12e7761d8 100644
--- a/target/riscv/tcg/cpu_helper.c
+++ b/target/riscv/tcg/cpu_helper.c
@@ -27,6 +27,7 @@
 #include "exec/page-protection.h"
 #include "exec/target_page.h"
 #include "system/memory.h"
+#include "system/physmem.h"
 #include "instmap.h"
 #include "tcg/tcg-op.h"
 #include "accel/tcg/cpu-loop.h"
@@ -1467,6 +1468,16 @@ static int get_physical_address(CPURISCVState *env, hwaddr *physical,
         if (old_pte != pte) {
             goto restart;
         }
+        /*
+         * The update went through the host pointer: log it, as a store would
+         * be, so dirty-memory clients (migration, in-memory snapshots that
+         * copy back only dirty pages) see that the page-table page changed.
+         * The code bit is left alone, as before: page tables aren't code.
+         */
+        physical_memory_set_dirty_range(memory_region_get_ram_addr(mr) + addr1,
+                                        sxlen_bytes,
+                                        memory_region_get_dirty_log_mask(mr) &
+                                        ~(1 << DIRTY_MEMORY_CODE));
         pte = updated_pte;
     }
 
